Z||000001||fix||12-04-2001||10:13 AM||||ummm, I think you forgot some info, but here's an overview of the auto to manual swap.  You need:<BR>-pedal assembly<BR>-clutch master cylinder<BR>-clutch line<BR>-shifter assembly<BR>-tranny, clutch and shift cables<BR>-computer from the manual car (i think)<P>you need to remove the steering column and take off the park/neutral safety switch.  When you've got the steering column out, swap the pedal assemblies. (easier said than done)  Everything else is pretty straight forward except if you are still using the wiring harness from the auto you will need to ground the park/neutral sensor that originally went to the auto tranny.  Otherwise your car won't even crank over.  ||||reg||1
